# The SHA-512 of bytes or a text, in hex, and a check of bytes against one. Ported from deck/deck/code/hash.ts
# (term-cli-in-term-0080): hashBuffer, hashText, verifyHash.
#
# The decisions:
#   - the digest is @term/base/cryptography/digest `sha512`, spelled as lowercase hex by @term/base/bytes `to-hex`, and
#     a text is hashed over its UTF-8 bytes (@term/base/bytes `from-text`), so the digest is the one base binds on
#     every backend (item term-self-host-001-1511, where node:crypto and node:fs were docked)
#   - all three tasks are async, as base's `sha512` is: `verify-hash` answered synchronously in the original
#     (decision 173 of the 001-finish-self-host change)
#   - `hash-file` is retired with no caller (decision 173): the only base route, `read-bytes`, answers the empty bytes
#     for a folder, an unreadable file or a file past node's 2 GiB, and a digest of those would be wrong without a raise

load @term/base/cryptography/digest
  find sha512

load @term/base/bytes
  find to-hex
  find from-text

task hash-buffer
  take data, like bytes
  like text
  mark async

  save digest, sha512(data)
  back to-hex(digest)

task hash-text
  take value, like text
  like text
  mark async

  save digest, sha512(from-text(value))
  back to-hex(digest)

task verify-hash
  take data, like bytes
  take expected, like text
  like boolean
  mark async

  save actual, hash-buffer(data)
  back is-equal(actual, expected)
